# Prompt for Muse

On this project Andrew assigned the roles: Cursor is the designer, Muse is the developer. Cursor writes the spec and the review. Muse implements that spec and does not redesign it.

Every user-facing reply that directs Muse, reviews Muse's work, or accepts a slice ends with a paste-ready prompt. An acceptance names the next slice. Filing `~/team/handoffs/` on SSH-Dev does not replace that prompt.

The prompt names the handoff file, the checkout `/Users/andrewgraves/Developer/OpenClaw-DEV`, what to change, what to leave alone, how to prove it, and how to hand it back (append to the same handoff, set Status and Owner now).

Do not commit, push, apply live database migrations, or touch Production inside that prompt unless Andrew has said so in the same task.
